Upstream:  https://github.com/gaucho-matrero/altoclef
Copyright: (c) 2020 Adris Jautakas and the AltoClef contributors
           (TacoTechnica, James Green, Marvion Kirito, and others)
License:   MIT -- see altoclef/LICENSE

This copy is a fork tracking Minecraft 26.1.2 / Fabric / Java 25.

The significant modifications are listed below. This list is a courtesy rather
than a license requirement (MIT asks only that the copyright notice be kept),
and it is not exhaustive -- `git log altoclef/` is the complete record.

Modifications made for burtcraft:

  ADDED    src/main/java/adris/altoclef/external/ExternalControlServer.java
           A localhost-only, newline-delimited-JSON TCP server (default port
           7440) that exposes AltoClef's command executor and live game state
           to an out-of-process controller. Registered as an ADDITIVE Fabric
           "client" entrypoint in fabric.mod.json; it modifies no existing
           AltoClef class. Also draws the optional on-screen intent HUD and
           owns the F1 manual-control toggle.

  ADDED    src/main/java/adris/altoclef/commands/PlaceCommand.java
           `@place <block>`, backed by PlaceBlockNearbyTask.

  ADDED    src/main/java/adris/altoclef/mixins/KeyboardInputLockMixin.java
           src/main/java/adris/altoclef/mixins/MouseInputLockMixin.java
           Suppress physical keyboard/mouse input while the bot is driving, so
           a human at the same machine cannot fight the bot for control. F1
           releases the lock.

  ADDED    src/main/java/adris/altoclef/mixins/MixinLocalPlayer.java
           src/main/java/adris/altoclef/mixins/ClientUIMixin.java
           Camera view-angle hooks (smoothed look / auto third-person) and HUD
           stack handling.

  ADDED    src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasks/misc/EatNowTask.java
           A user task that does nothing per tick. Its only job is to keep the
           TaskRunner enabled long enough for FoodChain to eat: see the
           TaskRunner note below for why that is necessary at all.

  ADDED    src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasks/construction/ToasterBuildTask.java
           src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasks/construction/settlement/*.java
           The settlement builder: one fixed ASCII floorplan (never a generated
           or growing one), laid bottom course first, with its own survey,
           restock and hand-placement recovery. ToasterGeometry holds the plan;
           the Node side holds a byte-identical copy so both agree on every
           block.

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/commandsystem/CommandExecutor.java
           Added a public getMod() accessor so the control server can read the
           live task chain (used for the "what am I doing right now" readout).

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/chains/FoodChain.java
           Added requestEat(AltoClef), which drives the chain's own fillup path
           so an external controller can make the bot eat what it is already
           carrying. Upstream has no such entry point: `@food <n>` means "end up
           holding n food", which is satisfied instantly when the food is
           already in the pack, so the bot reported eating while it starved.
           requestEat recomputes from the inventory rather than reading the
           _hasFood field, which is a cache written only inside getPriority()
           and is therefore stale whenever the runner is idle.

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasksystem/TaskRunner.java
           src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasksystem/TaskChain.java
           Added isActive(). tick() returns immediately while inactive, so NO
           chain runs -- not food, not defense -- and the runner is inactive
           whenever no user task is running. Anything poking a chain from
           outside the tick loop has to be able to ask whether that poke will
           ever be read.
           Added TaskChain.runsWhileIdle() (default false) and idle reflex
           ticking, so the survival chains keep running between user tasks.
           Finishing a job used to disable every chain, which left the bot with
           no defense, no eating and nothing to press respawn. setReflexesAllowed
           (false) is what makes F1 manual control inert again.

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/chains/MobDefenseChain.java
           src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasks/movement/RunAwayFrom*.java
           Commitment and anti-oscillation in the flee/fight decision: running
           away and the task that walks back could each undo the other at ~3s
           period, because the escape distance and the disengage distance close
           the loop outside the chain's own hysteresis. After repeated fresh
           escapes inside a window the bot fights instead -- except where
           fighting is genuinely wrong (creeper, warden-class, outnumbered, or
           low health). Water is never entered to escape.

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/chains/*.java
           src/main/java/adris/altoclef/tasks/**, trackers/, util/helpers/
           Survivability and observability work across the task tree: stall and
           wedge recovery, smelting and mining fixes, protected-block handling,
           and debug states on tasks that previously reported nothing at all (a
           task with no setDebugState is invisible by construction).

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/Debug.java
           The Debug.log* helpers were commented-out no-ops upstream, so their
           silence meant nothing. They log again.

  MODIFIED src/main/java/adris/altoclef/Settings.java
           `showTaskChains` now defaults to false. Upstream's task-tree dump is
           an unreadable spew over a live stream, and a regenerated settings
           file used to silently bring it back.

  MODIFIED src/main/resources/fabric.mod.json
           Registered the "client" entrypoint above; bumped the Minecraft /
           Java / Fabric Loader dependency floors for 26.1.2.

  MODIFIED build.gradle, gradle.properties, settings.gradle
           Retarget to Minecraft 26.1.2 (which ships unobfuscated, so there are
           no Yarn mappings and Loom has no remapJar task -- `jar` is already
           the shippable artifact). Baritone is jar-in-jar'd into the AltoClef
           jar so only one jar is ever deployed.


